   "title": "DLSSDetailer \u2014 how to use",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Not magic: a minor detailer/upscaler. It adds a small, measured amount of crispness; it does not invent features or change the subject. The fine texture is synthesised (enhancement), not reconstructed.\n\nDLSSDetailer \u2014 Upscale + Re-detail\n1. Load Video: pick your clip (needs the VideoHelperSuite pack).\n2. Load Neural Renderer: dlssnr-ft-real-v2.safetensors (put weights in your MLXDLSS_WEIGHTS / weights dir).\n3. Video Upscale: scale_factor 2 = most visible (1.5 faster); detail_strength 2 = visible crispness (1 subtle, 3 grainy).\n   NOTE: the re-detail SYNTHESISES plausible texture \u2014 it does not reconstruct the original detail.\n4. auto_mask none = runs with just the weights; set 'skin' for faces (downloads a face-parsing model).\n5. Hit Run. Output lands in output/mlxdlss/.\n6. MEMORY: ComfyUI buffers every frame in RAM (~frames x frame size). For long or high-res clips on a small machine, use the CLI instead: mlxdlss-video convert in.mp4 out.mp4 --scale 2 --detail-strength 2 --temporal (streams, ~2-4 GB)."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
